  "prefLabel": "Ed 1123.07 Scheduling of Alternative Dispute Resolution, Prehearing Conference, and Due Process Hearing",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1123.07 Scheduling of Alternative Dispute Resolution, Prehearing Conference, and Due Process Hearing.\n\n(a) At the time of the filing notice of a due process hearing complaint under Ed 1123.04, the parties shall notify the office of legislation and hearings of mutually agreeable dates on which the parties would be available for an optional alternative dispute resolution under Ed 1122, and for a prehearing conference and a hearing.\n\n(b) If the parties chose to engage in alternative dispute resolution the parties shall notify the office of legislation and hearings of mutually agreeable dates on which the parties would be available for mediation, a neutral conference, or a local school district alternative dispute resolution program.\n\n(c) The scheduling shall allow for the following:\n\n(1) A day for an alternative dispute resolution, if the parties so decide;\n\n(2) A half day for a prehearing conference; and\n\n(3) A minimum of 2 days for a hearing.\n\nSource. (see Revision Note at chapter heading for Ed 1100) #9197, eff 6-28-08; ss by #12141, eff 3-24-17",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1100.html"
